From: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 11:08:04 +0200
Subject: drm/msm/dp: handle the HPD replug interrupt

Linux 7.2 leaves DP_DP_HPD_REPLUG_INT_MASK unhandled even though the
controller still reports it. Send disconnect and reconnect notifications
so userspace reprobes the RA620 downstream sink after monitor power-up.

Fixes: 5043357e75ba ("drm/msm/dp: rework HPD handling")
Signed-off-by: SuperKali <hello@superkali.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -943,6 +943,13 @@ static irqreturn_t msm_dp_display_irq_thread(int irq, void *dev_id)
 		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
 				      connector_status_connected);
 
+	if (hpd_isr_status & DP_DP_HPD_REPLUG_INT_MASK) {
+		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
+				      connector_status_disconnected);
+		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
+				      connector_status_connected);
+	}
+
 	/* Send HPD as connected and distinguish it in the notifier */
 	if (hpd_isr_status & DP_DP_IRQ_HPD_INT_MASK)
 		drm_bridge_hpd_notify(dp->msm_dp_display.bridge,
